<!--
    kuna: a signed read of an expression that prints as unsigned.

    The constant of `a0 - 1` is marked `1U` (markExplicitUnsigned) when its
    type is unsigned and a0 is not, which makes the C expression unsigned while
    the value keeps the signed type a sign extension, an arithmetic right
    shift, a signed compare or a signed divide reads it as.  Those readers
    added no cast, so the printed C read the value as unsigned: bitmask
    printed `(unsigned long)(long)(a0 - 1U) >> 6`, a zero extension, and
    bitmask(0) returned 0x8000000003ffffff where the binary returns
    0x83ffffffffffffff.  A signed reader of such an expression now casts it to
    the signed integer of its size.

    Source (gcc 11 -O2 x86-64, .text bytes verbatim):
        UL bitmask(int s) { int t = s - 1; return ((UL)(L)t >> 6) | (1UL << (t & 63)); }
        int sigmember(const UL *set, int sig)          (control: no `U`)
        L sshift(int s) { int i = s - 1; return (L)(i >> 3) + (L)(U)(i & 63); }
        L sless(int s) { int i = s - 1; return (L)(i < 5) + (L)(U)(i & 63); }
        L sdiv(int s) { int i = s - 7; return (L)(i / 3) + (L)(U)(i & 63); }
        L ucmp(U a) { U t = a + 2; return (4 < t) + (L)(int)t; }
    ucmp is the control for the unsigned reader: its compare keeps `a0 + 2U`.

    Stage: P9 cast placement (ActionSetCasts; p9_emit/kuna_signedread.rs).
    Correctness fix, no option: #1-#5 fail on the unpatched engine, #6 holds
    before and after.
-->
